      "text": "First, we note that the equation $z^{28} - z^{8} - 1 = 0$ implies $z^{8}(z^{20} - 1) = 1$. Let $w = z^8$, so $w(z^{12} - 1) = 1$. Let $v = z^{12}$, so $v - 1 = w$, and therefore $v(w + 1) = 1$. Since $|z| = 1$, we have $0 < v < w < 1$.\n\nFinally, we have $v(v - w) = 1$, which gives us $(v + w + 2v)(v + w - v) = (v + w + 2v)^2 = 4v^2 = 1$. Hence, $v + w = \\frac{1}{2}$.\n\nPutting this together, we have $z^{12} = \\frac{1}{2},$ $z^{24} = \\frac{1}{4},$ $z^{28} = \\boxed{\\frac{1}{8}}$, and $z^{32} = \\frac{1}{8}$. \n\nTherefore, $z_3 = \\frac{1}{8}$.\n\nWe have $z_3 = w + \\frac{1}{2} = \\cos120^\\circ + i\\sin120^\\circ + \\frac{1}{2} = \\boxed{\\frac{1 + \\sqrt{3}}{2}}$. The answer is 472",
